    <DataNode elementId="AT4G34520-MONOMER" textLabel="very-long-chain 3-keto-acyl synthase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q38860" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The seeds of |FRAME: TAX-3702| contain approximately 28% (w/w of total fatty acids) of very-long-chain fatty acids (VLCFAs), and the most common of those is |FRAME: CPD-12189| (20:1). VLCFAs are synthesized as acyl-CoAs by the endoplasmic reticulum-localized elongase multiprotein complex |CITS: [9263455]|. The so-called &quot;condensing enzymes&quot; are components of the elongase complex that catalyze the first reaction of the elongase cycle in which the two carbons that originate from |FRAME: MALONYL-COA| are condensed to the growing acyl-CoA moiety |CITS: [9211877]|. Studies have shown that in yeast two different condensing enzymes participate in the elongase complex, each with different specificity for the length of the acyl moiety. In |FRAME: ORG-5993| there appear to be even more enzymes that fulfil this role. 20 putative genes encoding for such enzymes have been identified |CITS: [16765910]|. The |FRAME:AT4G34520| gene from |FRAME: ORG-5993| encodes a seed-specific elongase condensing enzyme that acts in conjunction with the 3-keto and trans-2,3-enoyl reductases of the elongase system |CITS: [16449229]|. The enzyme was expressed in Saccharomyces cerevisiae as a His&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;-N-terminal fusion protein, solubilized, and purified to near homogeneity |CITS: [12135493]|. The enzyme is active on both saturated and mono-unsaturated acyl-CoAs of 16 and 18 carbons, but its preferred substrate is |FRAME: OLEOYL-COA| (C18:1), resulting in the production of |FRAME: CPD-14291| (C20:1) at the end of the cycle (|FRAME: CPD-14293| (C22:1) is a minor product) |CITS: [9263455][12135493][16765910]|. Even though |FRAME:AT4G34520| is not homologous to the |FRAME: G-15115| and |FRAME: G-15116| enzymes from yeast |CITS: [7734965]|, expression of the Arabidopsis gene in yeat rescues the lethality of an |FRAME: G-15115|/|FRAME: G-15116| yeast double mutant |CITS: [16449229]|. Introduction of |FRAME:AT4G34520| alone into tissues of Arabidopsis and tobacco where significant quantities of VLCFAs are not found naturally was sufficient for the production and accumulation of VLCFAs |CITS: [9263455 ]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G34520-MONOMER" />
